  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Ball thieves",
  "description": "An area of roughly 30 × 15 metres is split into three parts: the blue den at one end, a middle area and the red den at the other end. All the balls start in the blue den. Two teams of four.\n\nBlue each take a ball and dribble out into the middle, where they try to keep it. Red are thieves who try to steal balls from blue and dribble them into their own den. A blue player who loses their ball runs home for a new one. Time how long it takes red to get every ball across, then swap jobs.\n\nHarder for the thieves: blue may also try to win a ball back before it reaches the red den. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Run at the player with the ball and slow down over the last few steps."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stand slightly side-on with one foot in front of the other and knees bent."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Take the ball when it gets a little too far from the attacker's foot."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 1,
